{"id": "makercfalse", "title": "makercfalse  a build that FAILED reported MAKE_RC=0 -- cause NOT established", "state": "open", "witness": "*** CORRECTED 2026-08-29 (L4).  THIS FIELD SAID: \"harness:READ 2026-08-27. The row had an EMPTY note; this is the first evidence on it. `regress/build_asan.sh` reports `make rc=$?` inside an `echo` and never asserts on it; its pass/fail decision is `\" -- and it is wrong in FOUR ways, each verified by opening the file. ***  (1) build_asan.sh is invoked as a FILE, so the wsl -c dollar-stripping cannot reach it at all.  (2) its rc sits BEFORE the find substitution in the same word, and expansion is left-to-right, so the rc printed IS make's (measured both orderings: before gives 1, after gives 0).  (3) the existence check is SOUND because build_one() wipes the directory first AND the gxemul link is the last action of `make all`, so existence is equivalent to make succeeding.  (4) 'Called by gate_asan_sweep.sh' is FALSE: that gate references it three times -- one gate_skip guard, two comments -- and no committed caller invokes it.  **AND THE POLARITY IS BACKWARDS: on 2026-08-28 the existence check this field condemns is what CAUGHT failed builds while MAKE_RC read 0.**  harness:regress/artifacts/makercfalse/wsl_dollar_20260829.out -- sections A-F, controls in both directions, ending MAKERC_SECTION_F_DONE.  Honest residual: the printed rc is informational and nothing asserts on it, which costs nothing with the directory wiped first."}
