{"id": "gdromwarnbits", "state": "in work", "witness": "detector:regress/artifacts/gdromwarnbits/bound_assert_controls.sh -- the COMPILE-TIME bound assert gdrom_w_fits_its_carriers, with a five-way control run preserved beside it. *** THIS FIELD READ `harness:` AND WAS MIS-FILED; corrected 2026-08-28 on the assess panel, where the fable5 seat named it. *** `harness:` is admitted only when the round's SUBJECT is the test apparatus, and this round's subject is PRODUCT code. The controls are two-sided on purpose: CLEAN on the shipped source and at nine bits over uint32_t, ERROR at nine over uint8_t, at 33 over uint32_t, and at 40 over uint64_t -- so the guard is demonstrably not a check that cannot fail. The superseded offline mask_equivalence_check.c remains as PROVENANCE only: two seats measured that it duplicates the definitions rather than including them, so it is an AUDIT of one moment and cannot see product drift. RUNG-3 ATTEMPT, per the 2026-08-27 lifecycle ruling: not applicable by construction -- the defect is a COMPILE-TIME representation bound, latent at six bits and unreachable by any guest access on HEAD.", "title": "gdromwarnbits  six of eight warn bits are used and they are hand-assigned hex masks; the ninth overflows a uint8_t SILENTLY and floods"}
