{"id": "offlinescope", "title": "offlinescope  The machine embargo was over-scoped: 11 of 14 offline differentials build and run in 10 seconds total, and six of the top eight ranked defects sit in files they already pull in", "state": "open", "witness": "harness:measured directly -- every differential compiled and run, timed. Re-derivable with one script; nothing touches a build tree, rig or wall-clock oracle."}
{"id": "asanstaletree", "title": "asanstaletree  build-asan/ carries pre-#427 copies of at least two device files, so any ASan measurement there measures code four rounds old", "state": "open", "witness": "harness:a direct file census -- line counts and round-tag greps across the four trees. Re-derivable in one command."}
{"id": "fbclearidempotent", "title": "fbclearidempotent  the DC21285 says a timer clear has no effect if the interrupt was already clear, but the write arm reloads a periodic timer unconditionally", "state": "open", "witness": "none yet -- researched, not reproduced.  The reproduction is specified and is offline-buildable in the EXISTING `diff_footbridge.c` fixture: set TIMER_MODE_PERIODIC, ensure pending == 0, write TIMER_1_CLEAR, and observe the counter reload.  A rung-3 attempt is OWED before the round records rung 1 (owner ruling 2026-08-27), and `cats` is a real in-tree ARM machine with this device, so it is plausibly buildable."}
{"id": "fbclearaliases", "title": "fbclearaliases  the four-address timer fold is READ from the code and is not detector-backed -- every #474 row exercises timer 1", "state": "open", "witness": "none -- filed, no work done yet."}
{"id": "bugfileledgerdir", "title": "bugfileledgerdir  precommit section P checks ledger -> OUTSTANDING_BUGS but NOTHING checks the reverse, and four rows were filed in prose only", "state": "open", "witness": "harness: the subject IS the checking apparatus, so the ladder's `harness:` term applies. Proof would be a mutation -- add a bugfile-only row and show the check reds."}
{"id": "wdcwidthmatrix", "title": "wdcwidthmatrix  the #475 detector covers access widths 4 and 2; the full width x remainder matrix and exact-fit controls are not shipped", "state": "open", "witness": "none -- completeness debt against a detector that is above the vacuity floor."}
{"id": "wdccdbaccum", "title": "wdccdbaccum  give the ATAPI CDB its own accumulator, as dev_mb89352.c does, instead of trigger-matching on a SHARED ring occupancy", "state": "open", "witness": "none -- structural, filed from two seats' reading of the in-tree precedent."}
{"id": "wdcaltfixture", "title": "wdcaltfixture  every alt-ctrl row runs in a state NO REAL DRIVER IS EVER IN, so eleven single-field qualifications escape the whole file", "state": "open", "witness": "none -- filed from a MEASURED escape set, no fix work done yet."}
{"id": "wdcaltwidth", "title": "wdcaltwidth  the alt-ctrl register's ACCESS WIDTH is unpinned: every row uses len == 1 while the region is registered TWO bytes wide", "state": "open", "witness": "none -- filed from a reading of the registration, no measurement yet."}
{"id": "wdcfloodstale", "title": "wdcfloodstale  `overrun x2` in wdc_flood_probe.py cannot reach its target since #479 reset the ring on every command", "state": "in work", "witness": "harness:mutation -- the re-aimed row reds under Mb2 (the producer's latch DELETED), 1,145,0 against want 1,1,0, measured on the shipped bytes.  The OLD row read 0 on that same mutant, so it was non-discriminating rather than merely red."}
{"id": "seatunfinished", "title": "seatunfinished  a seat that investigates and never concludes is scored 'answered, format miss' -- no answer recorded as bad formatting", "state": "open", "witness": "none -- filed from one measured instance, with the counter-instances named."}
{"id": "landiskaux", "title": "landiskaux  DEVINIT has no MACHINE_LANDISK case, so twelve measured Device Control writes land on unmapped memory -- one line, and now UNBLOCKED", "state": "open", "witness": "none -- filed; the mapping is unverified by any row because DEVINIT is invisible to the offline differential."}
{"id": "gdromdefaultstatusless", "state": "open", "witness": "none -- a harness gap, and the round's subject is the test apparatus", "title": "gdromdefaultstatusless  gdrom_default_probe.py's session() calls waitpid and DISCARDS the status, so NO row in 52 can tell a clean exit from a signal from a decline"}
{"id": "landiskunmapped4", "state": "open", "witness": "boot:landisk census, three boots, deterministic", "title": "landiskunmapped4  a landisk boot makes 26 unmapped accesses, deterministic across three boots, of which only ONE was previously carried -- the guest's whole external-interrupt setup is discarded"}
{"id": "hygienenonexistant", "state": "open", "witness": "harness:VERIFIED 2026-08-30 by grep, both directions.  `regress/gate_hygiene.sh` contains ZERO occurrences of `non-existant` AND zero of `non-existent`, so the gate looks for neither spelling.  Meanwhile `src/core/memory.c` EMITS the misspelled form at two sites, and the string appears across 16 files in `src/`.", "title": "hygienenonexistant  the boot-log hygiene gate does NOT look for `non-existant` at all -- 26 guest stores per landisk boot fall off the memory map and no gate says a word"}
{"id": "gdromlatchreuse", "state": "open", "witness": "detector:regress/gdrom_toclen_probe.py -- 19 rows, and the mutant escapes all of them", "title": "gdromlatchreuse  reusing GDROM_W_LEN instead of #489's new warn bit scores 19/19 -- the detector cannot see one latch bit standing in for another"}
{"id": "gdromonce", "state": "open", "witness": "none -- documented; a presence pin, not a code change", "title": "gdromonce  the `(once)` suppression marker is claimed in prose by the house idiom and pinned by no row in any gdrom probe"}
{"id": "asanbaselinedrift", "state": "open", "witness": "harness:build-asan/ was measured unbuildable while every commit's propagation check reported green", "title": "asanbaselinedrift  the propagation check is INCREMENTAL, so a stale BASELINE is invisible -- build-asan/ drifted until it would not compile while passing every commit"}
{"id": "gatebuildallow", "title": "gatebuildallow  gate_build.sh PINS its own twin-tree allowlist while est_divergence.txt exists to prevent exactly that -- one stale entry cost a RED weekly battery and a silently SKIPPED gate for five days", "state": "open", "witness": "harness:the 2026-08-23 battery verdict and log, plus a direct comparison of the two allowlists.  Preserved at _scratchpad/nightly/verdict_20260823_180000.txt and battery_20260823_180000.log."}
{"id": "gdromfmt24", "title": "gdromfmt24  the 0x24 data-format arm is left unlatched and unbounded beside a latched sibling, and its correctness is unsettleable without an SPI/GD-ROM doc", "state": "open", "witness": "none -- a DOCUMENTATION question, not an execution one.  The arm's behaviour is known and byte-identical to upstream; what is unknown is whether upstream is RIGHT, and no local manual covers GD-ROM/SPI/ATAPI packet commands."}
{"id": "gdromlatchcross", "title": "gdromlatchcross  two MEASURED 20/20 escapes past #490's detector: a one-character `|=` -> `=` that silently unlatches eight siblings, and an order-dependent latch widening", "state": "open", "witness": "none needed for the FILING -- both escapes are MEASURED, not predicted: p2askagain_20260829/ carries the scored logs with each mutant's row block byte-identical to base.  A FIX would owe its own witness."}
