74: 		 *  THE TODO THAT USED TO SIT HERE IS ANSWERED, 2026-08-22,
75: 		 *  against a real SH7750 Hardware Manual (Rev.7.00,
76: 		 *  REJ09B0366-0700) obtained by owner directive.  It asked
77: 		 *  whether URC should be left alone by `ldtlb`, wondered
78: 		 *  whether this was the right place, and floated setting it
79: 		 *  to a random value instead.  The MMUCR field definition
80: 		 *  settles all three:
81: 		 *
82: 		 *      "URC is incremented each time the UTLB is accessed.
83: 		 *       When URB > 0, URC is reset to 0 when the condition
84: 		 *       URC = URB occurs. ...  URC is not incremented by an
85: 		 *       LDTLB instruction."
86: 		 *
87: 		 *  So the suspicion was RIGHT and the random-value idea was
88: 		 *  WRONG -- and this code already conforms, by construction
89: 		 *  rather than by intent: X(ldtlb) in cpu_sh_instr.c reads
90: 		 *  URC out of MMUCR and indexes utlb_hi[]/utlb_lo[] itself,
91: 		 *  never entering this translation path, so no increment can
92: 		 *  happen there.  Nothing to change; the TODO simply never
93: 		 *  knew.  The wrap below also matches the quoted text.
94: 		 */
95: 		urb = (cpu->cd.sh.mmucr & SH4_MMUCR_URB_MASK) >>
96: 		    SH4_MMUCR_URB_SHIFT;
97: 		urc = (cpu->cd.sh.mmucr & SH4_MMUCR_URC_MASK) >>
98: 		    SH4_MMUCR_URC_SHIFT;
