8: What this protects
224:     ("fp in slot",   ["sr=0x400080f0", "put h 0x%x, 0xa002" % CODE,
352: #       instruction), and a TLB miss exception, protection violation exception,
365: #  Hence `sq pr00 rdok` and `sq d0 rdok`: in privileged mode a read is permitted
367: #  for what they now prove, because the old names -- "prot" and "clean" -- assert
368: #  a protection case and a dirty-bit case that read-type judgement does not have.
390: #  the `sq pr00 rdok` row.
576:     #  no protection case at PR=00 in privileged mode and no dirty-bit case at all.
586:     #  31.  Setting it here costs nothing (SQMD only bars USER access, and this
588:     #  mutant, which now judges PR=00 as a write and takes a protection
590:     ("sq pr00 rdok", sq_seq(sq_da1(pr=0), mmucr=MMUCR_AT | MMUCR_SQMD),
592:     ("sq d0 rdok",  sq_seq(sq_da1(d=0)),       DESTVIRT + 0xE0, FLUSHED),
594:     #  miss: the miss changes its CODE while prot and clean stop faulting entirely.
598:     ("sq pr00 evt", sq_seq_ev(sq_da1(pr=0)),   EVSCRATCH, NOEXC),
599:     ("sq d0 evt",   sq_seq_ev(sq_da1(d=0)),    EVSCRATCH, NOEXC),
